// Jobs lists the scheduled jobs of this service. This file is yours; devkit
// creates it once. A job is a function with a name and a cron schedule; the
// schedule lives here, next to the code, and the deployment turns the list
// into one Kubernetes CronJob per job (the CI runs `<binary> --list-jobs`
// after every build). Each run is `<binary> --job=<name>`: the framework
// opens what the configuration enables, gives the run a root span, a logger
// with job / run_id / trace_id, a lock against overlapping runs, the
// timeout, and exits with 1 on failure. Try one on your machine with
// `make job NAME=<name>`.
//
// Jobs is also called with an empty Runtime to print the list, so it must
// only register jobs: open nothing, query nothing, here.
//
// Rules for the function: idempotent and resumable (a run can be retried),
// work in chunks and commit each, check ctx.Err() between chunks, read the
// watermark from the data instead of trusting "last run time". Schedules
// are UTC, five fields. Names: lowercase letters, digits and dashes.
//
// Jobs 列出本服务的定时任务。本文件归你所有，devkit 只创建一次。一个任务就是一个带名字和
// cron 时间表的函数：时间表写在这里、和代码放在一起，部署会把清单变成一个任务一个
// Kubernetes CronJob（CI 每次构建后执行 `<二进制> --list-jobs`）。每次运行就是
// `<二进制> --job=<名>`：框架打开配置里启用的东西，给这次运行一个根 span、带 job / run_id /
// trace_id 的 logger、防重叠的锁和超时，失败以 1 退出。本机试跑：`make job NAME=<名>`。
//
// 打印清单时 Jobs 也会被一个空的 Runtime 调用，所以这里只能登记任务，不能打开或查询任何东西。
//
// 函数的规矩：幂等且可续跑（一次运行可能被重试），分块处理、每块提交，块之间看 ctx.Err()，
// 水位从数据里读而不是相信"上次运行时间"。时间表是 UTC、五段式。名字只用小写字母、数字和横线。
func Jobs(rt *kitexx.Runtime) []jobx.Job {
	_ = rt
	_ = time.Minute
	return []jobx.Job{
